{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:53:01.818Z","ordinal":34278,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19b3f-567a-7c11-9880-683af5154771","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- v1.1.2-release: state=Independent review REQUEST_CHANGES found installed package candidate runtime absent from sandbox mounts. Added failing CLI runtime-path assertion and non-empty external-package candidate regression; red reproduced provider requests=0. Fixed runVersionedEvalCommand to mount only <package>/lib/cli and <package>/lib/core while keeping package root evaluator closure unmounted. Focused CLI tests pass 7/7; external packaged regression now passes and hidden check correct=1. npm build passes. Full suite rerun started on synchronized snapshot; log /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot/wp1104-suite-ci-runtime-fix.log, SUITE claim held., phase=GREEN, gate=third full npm test active ~19m30s; T3 evaluator checks passed and suite is now in later worktree-bound agent tests; no failure summary; scope postcheck pending, next=Continue the active full run; collect final suite and scope-test outcome, friction=WP-1104 AC4 six-task installed-candidate acceptance awaits remote GATEWAY; WP-1105 claim owner Codex-GPT-6 has not responded and ten untracked files must be preserved, updated=2026-11-02T07:52:20Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta, verdict=APPROVED for runtime mount fix; suite and WP-1104 AC4 remain open, updated 1 minute ago\n- ...783 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 7:53am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (8,592t read) | 42,499t work | 80% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27058 5:44a ○ WP-1105 Has No Implementation Delta — Branch Claimed But No Code Changes\n27059 \" ○ WP-1105 Branch Has Untracked eval/evaluators/ Implementation — Not Committed\n27064 6:35a ○ Full Suite Re-run Completes: 2125/2129 Pass, 2 Failures\n27065 \" ○ Suite Failure Root Cause Analysis: cloud_providers and TUI E2E\n27066 6:36a ○ cloud_providers.test.ts Passes 44/44 in Isolation — Suite Failure is Node Runner IPC Flake\n27067 \" ○ SUITE Claim Scope Updated — TUI E2E Isolation Reproduction in Progress\n27068 6:37a ○ TUI E2E Test Passes 1/1 in Isolation — Suite Failure is a Timing Flake\n27069 \" ◆ Third Full Suite Run Started — Final Retry After Flake Isolation\n27070 \" ✓ Work State Updated to GREEN Phase for WP-1104 Gate\n27072 6:48a ○ Agent Mail Sent to /root/release_gate_audit\n27073 6:49a ○ Agent Mail Sent to /root/wp1105_spec_plan — WP-1105 Coordination Followup\n27077 \" ○ Sleep Interrupted by Incoming Agent Message\n27078 \" ○ Claims Log Reveals PR396 CI Status and Integration History\n27079 \" ⚖ GATEWAY_AC4_RULING_REQUEST Logged — WP-1104 AC4 Mock-Only Acceptance Does Not Need GATEWAY Claim\n27084 7:13a ○ Suite Child Process Stalled on do_get_write_access — Disk I/O Block\n27085 \" ○ retention.test.ts Worker Stalled on jbd2_log_wait_commit — ext4 Journal Flush\n27087 7:16a ○ System Under Sustained I/O Pressure — avg10=28% During retention.test.ts jbd2 Stall\n27088 7:17a ○ retention.test.ts Worker (PID 322836) Exited — jbd2 Stall Resolved After ~6 Minutes\n27092 7:30a ○ Third Full Suite Run Completes: 2134/2137 Pass, 1 Failure in sidecar.test.ts\n27093 \" ○ sidecar.test.ts Being Re-run in Isolation After Suite Completion\n27094 7:32a ○ sidecar.test.ts Passes 55/55 in Isolation — Suite Failure Confirmed as Timing Flake\n27095 \" ○ nexus-code Main Checkout Has 16 Modified Files — Dirty Working Tree Must Remain Untouched\n27096 \" ⚖ WP-1104 Gate Status: Two Retries Both Have Flake-Only Failures — Fresh Full Rerun Required\n27097 \" ◆ Fourth Full Suite Run Started — wp1104-suite-final3.log, Scope \"Rerun 3 After Isolated Failures Passed\"\n27101 7:49a ○ Fourth Suite Run at 17 Minutes — Current Test: agent_discovered_verifier_premutation\n\nAccess 42k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793605981.8182385,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
