{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:27:35.108Z","ordinal":35230,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c41791af-d813-4542-be5c-47877f3c340b","process_id":"58417","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,120p' scripts/package-linux.sh; rg -n 'package-linux' Makefile package.json cli/package.json | head -n 30; rg -n 'Bookworm|package-linux' docs/v1.0.0 docs/v1.1.0 | head -n 30"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,120p' scripts/package-linux.sh","name":"package-linux.sh","path":"scripts/package-linux.sh"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n package-linux Makefile package.json cli/package.json","query":"package-linux","path":"Makefile"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Bookworm|package-linux' docs/v1.0.0 docs/v1.1.0","query":"Bookworm|package-linux","path":"v1.0.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# An externally selected package tool may target a separate immutable RC checkout, but it must\n# still run from that checkout so version, source and lockfile identity stay bound together.\nROOT=${NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE:-$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)}\nROOT=$(cd \"$ROOT\" && pwd -P)\nif [[ -n \"${NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE:-}\" ]]; then\n  CALLER_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\n  SOURCE_ROOT=$(git -C \"$ROOT\" rev-parse --show-toplevel)\n  if [[ \"$ROOT\" != \"$CALLER_ROOT\" || \"$ROOT\" != \"$SOURCE_ROOT\" ]]; then\n    echo \"NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE must be the current Git worktree root\" >&2\n    exit 2\n  fi\nfi\nVERSION=${1:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nOUT=${2:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nAPPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE='rust:1.95.0-bookworm@sha256:4c2fd73ef19c5ef9d54bee03b06b2839a392604fbfcd578ed948b71b37c1d7fb'\ncase \"$VERSION\" in v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*) ;; *) echo \"version must look like v1.2.3\" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac\nif [[ -z \"${NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE:-}\" ]]; then\n  if [[ \"${NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD:-}\" != \"1\" ]]; then\n    echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder (set NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1 only for local development)\" >&2\n    exit 2\n  fi\nelif [[ \"$NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE\" != \"$APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE\" ]]; then\n  echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nmkdir -p \"$OUT\"\nOUT=$(cd \"$OUT\" && pwd -P)\nWORK=$(mktemp -d)\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$WORK\"' EXIT\n\nnpm --prefix \"$ROOT/cli\" ci\nnpm --prefix \"$ROOT/cli\" run build\n\nif [[ -n \"${NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE:-}\" ]]; then\n  if [[ ! \"$NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE\" =~ @sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$ ]]; then\n    echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must be pinned by sha256 digest\" >&2\n    exit 2\n  fi\n  command -v docker >/dev/null || { echo \"docker is required for the pinned Rust build image\" >&2; exit 2; }\n  mkdir -p \"$WORK/rust-build\"\n  docker run --rm --pull=always --platform linux/amd64 \\\n    --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" \\\n    --mount \"type=bind,src=$ROOT,dst=/nexus-source,readonly\" \\\n    --mount \"type=bind,src=$WORK/rust-build,dst=/nexus-build\" \\\n    --workdir /nexus-source \\\n    --env HOME=/tmp/nexus-package-build-home \\\n    --env CARGO_HOME=/nexus-build/cargo-home \\\n    --env CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/nexus-build/target \\\n    --env RUSTUP_HOME=/usr/local/rustup \\\n    \"$NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE\" \\\n    cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path /nexus-source/core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n  RUST_CORE_TARGET=\"$WORK/rust-build/target/release\"\nelse\n  cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path \"$ROOT/core/Cargo.toml\" --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n  RUST_CORE_TARGET=\"$ROOT/core/target/release\"\nfi\n\nPKG=\"$WORK/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PKG/bin\" \"$PKG/lib/core\" \"$PKG/lib/cli\"\ncp -R \"$ROOT/cli/dist\" \"$PKG/lib/cli/dist\"\ncp \"$ROOT/cli/package.json\" \"$ROOT/cli/package-lock.json\" \"$PKG/lib/cli/\"\nnpm ci --omit=dev --prefix \"$PKG/lib/cli\"\ncp \"$RUST_CORE_TARGET/harness-core\" \"$RUST_CORE_TARGET/nexus-tui\" \"$PKG/lib/core/\"\nnode \"$ROOT/scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\" \"$ROOT\" \"$PKG\"\ncommand -v readelf >/dev/null || { echo \"readelf is required to verify package glibc compatibility\" >&2; exit 2; }\nfor binary in \"$PKG/lib/core/harness-core\" \"$PKG/lib/core/nexus-tui\"; do\n  required_glibc=$(readelf --version-info --wide \"$binary\" | grep -oE 'Name: GLIBC_[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)+' | sed 's/.*GLIBC_//' | sort -V | tail -n 1)\n  if [[ -n \"$required_glibc\" ]]; then\n    IFS=. read -r glibc_major glibc_minor _ <<< \"$required_glibc\"\n    if (( glibc_major > 2 || (glibc_major == 2 && glibc_minor > 35) )); then\n      echo \"$binary requires GLIBC_$required_glibc, above the GLIBC_2.35 compatibility ceiling\" >&2\n      exit 1\n    fi\n  fi\ndone\ncp \"$ROOT/LICENSE\" \"$PKG/LICENSE\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$VERSION\" > \"$PKG/VERSION\"\n\nSOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git -C \"$ROOT\" log -1 --format=%ct)\nexport SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH\nGIT_COMMIT=$(git -C \"$ROOT\" rev-parse HEAD)\nBUILD_DATE=$(date -u -d \"@$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH\" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ 2>/dev/null || date -u -r \"$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH\" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nSTATE_SCHEMA_VERSION=$(node --input-type=module - \"$PKG/lib/cli/dist/core/state.js\" <<'EOF'\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nconst { CURRENT_STATE_SCHEMA_VERSION: version } = await import(pathToFileURL(process.argv[2]).href);\nif (!Number.isSafeInteger(version) || version < 1) throw new Error('packaged client has no valid state schema');\nprocess.stdout.write(String(version));\nEOF\n)\n\n# Embed the compatibility contract in the attested archive. The detached asset\n# adds the archive digest after the archive is built and is covered by SHA256SUMS.\ncat > \"$PKG/compatibility.json\" <<EOF\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"product\": \"nexus-code\",\n  \"version\": \"${VERSION#v}\",\n  \"revision\": \"$GIT_COMMIT\",\n  \"builtAt\": \"$BUILD_DATE\",\n  \"minimumUpdaterVersion\": \"0.1.0-alpha.2\",\n  \"components\": {\n    \"cli\": \"${VERSION#v}\",\n    \"core\": \"${VERSION#v}\",\n    \"tui\": \"${VERSION#v}\",\n    \"harness\": \"${VERSION#v}\"\n  },\n  \"compatibility\": {\n    \"configSchemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"stateSchemaVersion\": $STATE_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n    \"minSupportedConfigVersion\": 1,\n    \"minSupportedStateVersion\": 0\n  },\n  \"platforms\": {\n    \"linux-x86_64\": {\n      \"archive\": \"$ARCHIVE\",\n      \"os\": \"linux\",\nMakefile:41:\tNEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE=$(APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE) bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"v$$VERSION\" \"$$TMP1\" && \\\nMakefile:42:\tNEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE=$(APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE) bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"v$$VERSION\" \"$$TMP2\" && \\\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:19:**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:25:3. **Versioned runtime dispatch and packaged closure** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`; tests: `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner`, `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files`, `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`. First verify resolver/dispatch with a synthetic package; verify the staged allowlist excludes datasets/oracles; then build and stage the actual package and invoke the installed CLI outside the checkout against an empty benchmark split, exercising the real runner and scorer subprocesses without inference. Reconcile package allowlist changes against the current script rather than replaying historical packaging commits.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:36:- `scripts/package-linux.sh` claim was free before this slice took its claim.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:50:- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-package-reference`; query: \"package-linux.sh evaluator runtime allowlist copy eval run.mjs\"; hit `package-linux.sh:73`; retrieved the explicit runtime closure and exclusions for datasets, tests and held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:63:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:75:- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:34:| G1h | Packaging | `bash scripts/package-linux.sh` twice + byte comparison | identical tarball, `SHA256SUMS`, notices, SBOM, installer |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:16:**Two launchers.** The developer launcher is `harness.sh` (on this host, `/usr/local/bin/nexus`). With no arguments on a TTY it starts the Ratatui live TUI. The packaged launcher `bin/nexus` (`scripts/package-linux.sh:24-30`) is `node lib/cli/dist/index.js \"$@\"`. With no arguments it starts the readline REPL (`cli/src/index.ts:747-749`).\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:17:PR #374 (`bed30a90`). CI matrices (Node 22, 24), dual container packaging (`package-linux.sh`), bit-for-bit\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:114:| Packaging (`package-linux.sh` ×2), SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, `installer-smoke.sh` | not run |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:22:| Build entry points | `make build` (cargo release + `tsc`), `make test` (cargo test + `npm --prefix cli test` + `scripts/security_gates.sh`), `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/smoke-package.sh`, `scripts/installer-smoke.sh`. CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (contest contract job + `linux-x86_64`), `release.yml` (tag-triggered). A dead `.gitlab-ci.yml` also exists. | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:265:| REL-01 | S2 | B | Install → first run | `package-linux.sh:24-30`; `index.ts:747` | RT | The installed product lacks the TUI | REQ-REL-101 (SPEC-06) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:29:| scripts/package-linux.sh | targeted (packaged bin/nexus) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:43:- Entry points: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js \"$@\"` (package-linux.sh:25-30); no args -> `repl`\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:60:| TUI-04 | S2 | Install -> first run | scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30; index.ts:747; live.rs:126-131; tui.ts:59-90 | SOURCE+RUNTIME: packaged `nexus` = REPL; no command reaches the live TUI; packaged `lib/core/nexus-tui --live` fails \"sidecar not found at <pkg>/cli/dist/sidecar.js\" (checkout-layout assumption `ancestors().nth(4)`). ISSUE12 UI-004 (\"TUI MUST serve as the default interactive human surface\" — Satisfied) is false for the shipped package | Release users get the weaker REPL (TUI-02/03/08 apply) and never the hardened TUI | Make `nexus` launch `nexus-tui --live` on a TTY with packaged sidecar path; resolve packaged layout |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:12:- `scripts/package-linux.sh`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:37:| 7 | Installer: strict tag regex; `-fsSL --show-error`; no-stable-release hint naming the latest prerelease; rate-limit message; `MANIFEST.sha256` repair on reinstall; `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. | `install.sh:21-49`; `package-linux.sh` (write manifest) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:19:- `harness.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh` (CA export)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:37:| 12 | Custom CA: document `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` in config.env; the launcher (node entry re-exec, or `bin/nexus` sh) exports it before node starts; doctor validates that the file exists and parses. | `scripts/package-linux.sh:24-30` launcher; `harness.sh`; `doctor.ts` | PLAN-06 task 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:14:| scripts/package-linux.sh, smoke-package.sh, installer-smoke.sh, package-smoke-*.{py,mjs}, security_gates.sh, audit_rust_deps.py, generate_sbom.sh, token_accounting.py | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:32:- **Release pipeline.** A tag `v*.*.*` triggers `release.yml`. The workflow checks that the tag commit is an ancestor of origin/main and that the tag matches `package.json` version. It then runs `npm ci`, the cli build, `cargo test --locked`, the release build, `npm test`, and security_gates. Next it runs `package-linux.sh` twice and `cmp`s the outputs (a reproducibility check), then `smoke-package.sh` and `installer-smoke.sh`. Finally `softprops/action-gh-release` uploads `nexus-linux-x86_64-<tag>.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS`, setting prerelease when the tag contains `-`. Release notes come from `generate_release_notes`; `docs/releases/*.md` is not used.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:59:| REL-01 | S2 | install → first run | scripts/package-linux.sh:24-30; cli/src/index.ts:747-749; harness.sh:21-38 | RUNTIME. Installed `nexus` (no args) opens the readline REPL. `nexus --live` → `error: unknown option '--live'`. The packaged launcher has no route to the live TUI (`nexus-tui --live --sidecar`), although nexus-tui and sidecar.js are shipped and doctor reports `PASS tui.build: The live TUI ... built`. | Release users never get the primary UI that the developer uses and that the PTY tests cover. The shipped product is a different product from the tested daily driver. The doctor's PASS is misleading. | Make the packaged launcher equal to harness.sh: same routing, and live TUI when there are no args and a TTY. Add a smoke test that the package launches `--live` in a PTY. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:63:| REL-05 | S2 | compliance | scripts/package-linux.sh:22; release assets | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates are statically linked (Cargo.lock: 152 packages, MIT/Apache-2.0 etc.), and there is no third-party notice for them. Node deps ship their own LICENSE files (20 found). No SBOM is published. | MIT/Apache attribution obligations are not met for redistributed binaries. Enterprise intake (SBOM) is blocked. | Generate THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES (cargo-about / cargo-deny licenses + npm license list) and a real lockfile-based SBOM, and attach both to releases. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:74:| MNT-03 | S4 | maintainability | Makefile:36-45 | SOURCE. `verify-reproducibility` writes fixed `/tmp/nexus-repro-{1,2}` and covers only cli/dist, not the release tarball. The real check lives in the workflows (`cmp` of two package builds, same machine and same toolchain). | Weak local repro check. Cross-machine reproducibility is not proven. | Point the target at `package-linux.sh` twice + `cmp`, using mktemp. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:10:- `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`, `scripts/security_gates.sh`, `scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:26:| 2 | Third-party notices: install cargo-about and the npm license checker in CI. Use `about.toml` with an allowlist (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3, ISC, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, MPL-2.0 only if reviewed). Have `package-linux.sh` write `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` and upload it as an asset. | `package-linux.sh:22`; `release.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:32:| 8 | Delete `.gitlab-ci.yml`. Remove tracked `*.pyc` and ignore them. Point `make verify-reproducibility` at `package-linux.sh` run twice with mktemp and cmp. | `.gitlab-ci.yml`; `experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/harness/__pycache__`; `Makefile:36-45` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:15:- `scripts/package-linux.sh` (deterministic packaging of compatibility metadata with reproducible timestamps)\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:17:| REL-05 | The release archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates (MIT/Apache-2.0 and others) are statically linked into `harness-core` and `nexus-tui`, with no attribution. No SBOM is published. | RUNTIME + SOURCE (`scripts/package-linux.sh:22`) |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":196719792}},"started_at_ms":1793608053908,"completed_at_ms":1793608055108}}
