{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:28:08.484Z","ordinal":36827,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3715c0e2-ce99-4619-aa7b-0276316d02fb","process_id":"65431","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short; git log -5 --oneline --decorate; rg -n 'WP-110[1-8]|v1\\.1\\.2|ready|active|done' docs/v1.1.0 docs/releases/v1.1.2.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short; git log -5 --oneline --decorate; rg -n 'WP-110[1-8]|v1\\.1\\.2|ready|active|done' docs/v1.1.0 docs/releases/v1.1.2.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" M cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs\n M cli/src/index.ts\n M eval/README.md\n M eval/run.mjs\n M scripts/package-linux.sh\n?? cli/src/eval_cli.ts\n?? cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\n?? eval/package_runtime.test.mjs\n?? scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\n00a8cb4d (HEAD -> v1/v112-wp1104-integration) feat(eval): expose isolated versioned runner API\n6adbeb31 feat(eval): add versioned dataset runner integration\n593d569b (v1/v112-wp1106-planning) Merge pull request #397 from mikeholownych/v1/agent-skills-vercel-integration\n0965bcde (pr397-review) feat(skills): load Agent Skills from .agents/skills, follow symlinks, parse block-scalar frontmatter\n9a62db99 Merge pull request #395 from mikeholownych/v1/alerts-51-23-24\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.1.2\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:3:**Nexus Code v1.1.2** is a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:9:When a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:18:The v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:26:Operation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No migration runs, and v1.1.1 can read records written by v1.1.2.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:30:This release inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record and is the version-only promotion of `v1.1.2-rc.1`. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Its qualification is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of the candidate.\ndocs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json:68:            \"ready\",\ndocs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json:83:            \"ready\": {\ndocs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md:207:would invert the dependency (view already imports operation). Implement the length function in the scheduler and\ndocs/v1.1.0/MULTI_AGENT_ORCHESTRATION.md:34:4. **Role specialization as a first-class pattern** (already expressible, now tested): `role` selects requirements,\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:32:| 5. Release preparation and publication | candidate ready on `origin/main` `bed30a90`; handover to owner for tag/push/publication |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:1:# WP-1104: Standalone `nexus eval` command\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:17:**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset and runner foundation at `6adbeb31` and `00a8cb4d` on this branch. WP-1102 is not a functional dependency. WP-1108 is not imported as a branch; package changes will be based on the selected current package script and separately checked against its ownership and gate state.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:19:**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:26:4. **Installed candidate acceptance** — files: `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts` and the WP-1103 acceptance evidence path when claimed; test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. Require six unique manifest IDs, an invocation and validator result for each, zero skips/missing, candidate binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:28:**Reference corpora:** `nexus-cli` for Commander registration and CLI command dispatch; `nexus-test` for CLI command test patterns; `nexus-wp1104-reference` for the prior WP-1104 resolver and runtime behavior; `nexus-docs` for evaluation acceptance and dataset contracts.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:30:**Risk / unknowns:** The current package script must contain the evaluator closure needed by WP-1105. Retrieval query: \"which evaluator modules are copied into the Linux package and how are runtime paths resolved?\" The installed artifact test is the acceptance gate for this boundary.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:37:- WP-1108 triage at `v1/wp-1108-dependency-modernization` says its added CI job has not run at that branch head and its policy batch is not accepted; no WP-1108 packaging changes are treated as a qualified prerequisite.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:66:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:72:- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:76:- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:77:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:80:- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:81:- A separate focused test process in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr398-review` remains active. The next full-suite attempt must wait for it to finish, then set `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` to the freshly extracted development package so the actual outside-checkout runtime test runs instead of skipping.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:83:- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:63:| **Dependency Hygiene & Deprecations** | Proprietary managed bundle | IDE-integrated dependencies | Standard package requirements | **Zero Deprecated Packages Policy: 100% active upstream deps, automated deprecation CI gates** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:118:  - **Human Review Annotation Queue:** Multi-agent outputs merge cleanly into interactive review queues (`eval/annotations/queue.jsonl`), enabling human-in-the-loop oversight.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:122:- **The Problem:** The deployment of AI-generated code introduces legal, copyright, and security risks. Enterprise compliance requires proof of provenance and absence of unmaintained or abandoned code.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:152:  - **GBNF-Constrained API Schemas:** Enterprise action schemas compile directly into Context-Free Grammars (`WP-1107`), enforcing JSON schema compliance and valid parameter emission on supported local engines during multi-argument external calls.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:207:| **Interactive TUI Trace Inspector** | `v1.2.0` | [`ROADMAP.md`](./ROADMAP.md) §3 | Real-time visual drill-down into tool executions and token latencies |\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:39:  different keys to run concurrently.\" The coordinator exposes `active`, `isActive`, `run`, `wake`, `interrupt`,\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:60:  rather than reinterpret it; never replay a migration that already applied. In Nexus this becomes: one version step,\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:94:  matching the existing `DecisionAction` vocabulary. A transient provider fault is already classified as\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:141:**Evidence.** `docs/v1.1.0/README.md:28` already requires this for any `DurableOperationState` change; the rule was\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:166:**Evidence.** SPEC §3.2; the view already computes the same chain (`operation_view.ts:265-304`) and the task requires\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:176:invert the module dependency (`operation_view.ts` already imports `operation.ts`). The two measure different things on\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:218:**Alternative rejected.** A dependency-ordered queue. Dependency order is already enforced by the scheduler (a\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:315:2. `AbortSignal` propagation into the executor already works per turn (`UnitRunContext.signal`); concurrency does not\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:23:                                    - Dependabot Modernization (WP-1108)│\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:44:| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:45:| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:46:| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:47:| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:48:| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:49:| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:51:| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:61:### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:100:- **PR #120:** `ora` (8.2.0 → 9.4.1 in `/cli`) — Terminal spinner library update. Validate stdout/stderr streaming, non-interactive CI fallback, and Ratatui TUI coexistence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:108:**Theme:** Diagnostic reproducibility, statistical comparison across agent versions, interactive TUI trace inspection, and human annotation workflows.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:116:| **WP-1203** | **Interactive TUI Trace Inspector** | Add a hierarchical trace inspector panel to `nexus-tui` (Ratatui), allowing operators to view the tool call tree, intermediate stdout, and latency distributions. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:117:| **WP-1204** | **Human Review & Annotation Queue** | Implement `nexus review <session-id>`: Interactive CLI / TUI prompt guiding reviewers through structured rubrics (tool correctness, intent fulfillment) and recording signed audit evidence. | `REQ-AGT-010`, `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:150:   - Every npm dependency and Cargo crate must be on active, supported upstream releases.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:63:| Slice 1 read-only view shipped | `cli/src/operation_view.ts` (585 lines); `status --dag`, `--dag --json`, `watch`; `docs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json` | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:65:| View writes no transition | Test asserts sha256 + mtime unchanged across `status --dag` and `--dag --json` (`operation_view.test.ts:419-441`) | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:74:| Per-unit worktree/branch, integration at completion, receipts | `cli/src/core/operation_git.ts:180-229` (prepare), `:235-382` (integrate), receipts in `DurableOperationState.integrations` (`operation.ts:238-249`) | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:75:| `MERGE_CONFLICT` / `INTEGRATION_FAILED` decisions | `operation_runner.ts:264-289` | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:76:| Recovery: idempotent integration, receipt reconciliation, missing-worktree fail-closed | `operation_git.ts:238-333,445-468`; `operation_runner.ts:109-126,350-368` | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:87:| Per-unit context budget, pre-inference, blocks with `CONTEXT_BUDGET` | `operation_runner_execution.ts:152-187`; `unit.context` recorded at `:154-160` | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:90:| Durable hash-checked checkpoints with backup, lock, path-safe names | `operation_checkpoints.ts:66-254`; CLI `operation_cli.ts:240-334` | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:136:| OBS-1 | Read-only view (DAG, resources, events, critical path) | §7.1 | — | already covered | Existing 29 view tests | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:145:| GIT-1 | Opt-in per-unit isolation | §5.1 | — | already covered | 34 git tests | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:147:| GIT-3 | Conflict policy parks with an existing decision kind | §5.4 | — | already covered | `operation_git.test.ts:298-323` | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:157:| CTX-1 | Per-unit context budget | §6.1 | — | already covered | 20 context tests | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:161:| CTX-5 | Durable context checkpoints | §6.4 | — | already covered | 20 context tests | Already satisfied |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:170:| MAO-4 | Verification edges (implementer → tester → reviewer) | §3.6 | WP-2 | ACC-V11-MAO-06 | Failing review ends BLOCKED, never COMPLETE | Already satisfied + tests |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:188:| WP-1101 | OpenTelemetry-shaped local tracing (`trace.jsonl`) | None with `OperationEvent`; a separate trace format | **Defer**: needs its own spec and privacy review (trace content is agent output) |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:189:| WP-1102 | Flight-recorder credential redaction | Redaction already exists (`redactForPersistence`, `safeTerminal`) | **Investigate**: verify the existing redaction against the CRED003 fixtures before adding a second mechanism |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:190:| WP-1103 | Versioned eval datasets (`eval/datasets/`) | None | **Defer**: held-out custody (issue #1) is still unresolved; restructuring datasets now would disturb it |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:191:| WP-1104 | `nexus eval` command | None | **Defer**: depends on WP-1103 and the frozen thresholds |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:192:| WP-1105 | Modular code evaluators | The evaluator lives in `eval/` | **Defer**: depends on WP-1103 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:193:| WP-1106 | `--step` single-step loop | None | **Investigate**: small and independent; needs a decision on interaction with durable turns |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194:| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:195:| WP-1108 | Dependency modernization (27 Dependabot PRs) | `origin/main` already merged several (#103–#129 partially) | **Partly already satisfied**; the rest is dependency work, not a v1.1 feature |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:208:1. **The schema rule was already violated.** `docs/v1.1.0/README.md:28` requires a schema version and migration for\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:219:   nothing about what is already running. Without a reservation step, two units would be assigned the same\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:1:# WP-1103: Versioned Dataset Oracle Isolation\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:18:**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset loader and runner integration; current runner claims are held by root after the prior claim was recorded stale and broken; a test seam for AC1, AC2 and AC4. AC5 requires an integrated exact-candidate benchmark run and is separate from the unit regression suite; packaged installed CLI behavior depends on WP-1104.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:20:**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:56:- **Scope:** Live operator sessions, interactive runs, autonomous tasks.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:106:  \"objective\": \"Verify that detached legacy client restore does not overwrite active leases.\",\ndocs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md:16:  for downstream units already existed before this work.\ndocs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md:84:- Token estimates are already heuristic; changing the budget model can shift every qualification timing. Record the\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:35:Nexus already produces structured turn data (`turn.execution`, `turn.outcome`, `turn.reason`, `turn.steps`) via `AutonomousAgent.runTurn`. LangSmith's trace model is a superset of this, organized hierarchically as runs within threads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:37:**Relevance to Nexus:** Nexus's `turn.ts` and `agent.ts` already emit structured per-turn events. Adopting a trace/span model (similar to OpenTelemetry semantics) would let Nexus capture the full execution tree of a turn — not just the final outcome, but every tool call, schema repair, and verifier invocation as nested spans.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:66:**Relevance to Nexus:** Nexus's `eval/score.mjs` already produces pooled metrics (`correct`, `rate`, `ci`, `falseVerified`), but lacks experiment versioning and side-by-side comparison. Adopting the experiment model would let Nexus:\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:86:Nexus's `eval/run.mjs` already performs offline evaluation against `eval/tasks/`. LangSmith's model adds:\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:92:Nexus already runs 5 runs per task configuration (per DEC-05 thresholds) and measures false VERIFIED = 0, crash rate ≤ 2%, regression rate ≤ 5%. These map directly to LangSmith's offline evaluation model.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:108:LangSmith defines five evaluator types. Nexus already uses some implicitly; formalizing them would improve evaluation rigor.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:118:**Nexus parallel:** `repairJson` validation, `isKnownToolName` checks, `ALL_DIGITS_RE` validation. These are already implicit code evaluators but could be formalized as first-class evaluator functions with named scores.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:205:**Relevance to Nexus:** Rules could auto-escalate failing runs to an annotation queue, or trigger re-runs of failed tasks on infrastructure failures (Nexus already has `eval/infra.mjs` for this).\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:320:Nexus already has strong foundations (eval harness, scoring, independent acceptance). Adopting LangSmith's structured model — particularly versioned datasets, experiment comparison, annotation queues, and online evaluation — would move Nexus from ad-hoc qualification to a continuous quality assurance system suitable for production LLM agent deployment.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:86:  - `nexus.compaction.preserved_items_count`: Count of active messages retained\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:193:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:254:nexus replay <trace-id> [--verify-only] [--interactive]\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:30:| TUI operation pane and in-view decision interaction | Needs the Ratatui surface and a PTY qualification matrix; the CLI view already covers the operator need | v1.2 (DEC-V11-14) |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:45:2. Verifier and baseline gates: no unit completes without the evidence the unit model already requires.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:179:reserved = Map<resourceId, count>          // seeded with the slots already held by RUNNING units\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:216:| Scheduler exception | The batch is abandoned; every unit still `RUNNING` is reconciled by the next `run()`; the operation blocks with `NOT_CONVERGING` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:279:| non-integer / negative | The envelope gate already treats the record as corrupt; the operation gate MUST also reject it rather than assume 1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:296:    // absent v1.1 fields stay absent; readers already use ?? [] / ?? 1 defaults\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:307:- No unit is rewritten. `contextBudget`, `context`, `git`, `integrations` and `contextCheckpoints` already load\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:311:The envelope migration backup already applies because the envelope version is unchanged; therefore the operation\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:508:  **resume**, the undelivered set is re-rendered; a message already delivered is not repeated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:623:`mergeOperationPolicy` (`operation_cli.ts`) already merges config + spec. The new key follows the same precedence:\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:38:All G1 checks run under `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` / isolated `XDG_*` per CONCURRENCY §3; `npm --prefix cli test` already\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:12:conflict policy. `CandidateIdentity` already computed a content-addressed view of the working tree, which is the\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:32:   a time, in arrival order (v1.1.0: `OperationRunner.enqueueIntegration`). Dependency order is already guaranteed by\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:36:   `candidate`/`tests` when the worktree was already gone or the unit produced no verifier — an absent field is honest\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:56:- Integration must not bypass the verification gates: a unit is integrated only with the evidence the unit model already\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":920261908}},"started_at_ms":1793611687563,"completed_at_ms":1793611688484}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:28:10.233Z","ordinal":36828,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19b96-70f9-74c1-81d0-00ee506aeb71","call_id":"call_964f0cb20c664cf5ab88c761e99478b5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7121)\nTotal output lines: 128\n\n M cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs\n M cli/src/index.ts\n M eval/README.md\n M eval/run.mjs\n M scripts/package-linux.sh\n?? cli/src/eval_cli.ts\n?? cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\n?? eval/package_runtime.test.mjs\n?? scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\n00a8cb4d (HEAD -> v1/v112-wp1104-integration) feat(eval): expose isolated versioned runner API\n6adbeb31 feat(eval): add versioned dataset runner integration\n593d569b (v1/v112-wp1106-planning) Merge pull request #397 from mikeholownych/v1/agent-skills-vercel-integration\n0965bcde (pr397-review) feat(skills): load Agent Skills from .agents/skills, follow symlinks, parse block-scalar frontmatter\n9a62db99 Merge pull request #395 from mikeholownych/v1/alerts-51-23-24\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.1.2\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:3:**Nexus Code v1.1.2** is a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:9:When a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:18:The v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:26:Operation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No migration runs, and v1.1.1 can read records written by v1.1.2.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:30:This release inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record and is the version-only promotion of `v1.1.2-rc.1`. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Its qualification is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of the candidate.\ndocs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json:68:            \"ready\",\ndocs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json:83:            \"ready\": {\ndocs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md:207:would invert the dependency (view already imports operation). Implement the length function in the scheduler and\ndocs/v1.1.0/MULTI_AGENT_ORCHESTRATION.md:34:4. **Role specialization as a first-class pattern** (already expressible, now tested): `role` selects requirements,\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:32:| 5. Release preparation and publication | candidate ready on `origin/main` `bed30a90`; handover to owner for tag/push/publication |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:1:# WP-1104: Standalone `nexus eval` command\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:17:**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset and runner foundation at `6adbeb31` and `00a8cb4d` on this branch. WP-1102 is not a functional dependency. WP-1108 is not imported as a branch; package changes will be based on the selected current package script and separately checked against its ownership and gate state.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:19:**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:26:4. **Installed candidate acceptance** — files: `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts` and the WP-1103 acceptance evidence path when claimed; test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. Require six unique manifest IDs, an invocation and validator result for each, zero skips/missing, candidate binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:28:**Reference corpora:** `nexus-cli` for Commander registration and CLI command dispatch; `nexus-test` for CLI command test patterns; `nexus-wp1104-reference` for the prior WP-1104 resolver and runtime behavior; `nexus-docs` for evaluation acceptance and dataset contracts.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:30:**Risk / unknowns:** The current package script must contain the evaluator closure needed by WP-1105. Retrieval query: \"which evaluator modules are copied into the Linux package and how are runtime paths resolved?\" The installed artifact test is the acceptance gate for this boundary.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:37:- WP-1108 triage at `v1/wp-1108-dependency-modernization` says its added CI job has not run at that branch head and its policy batch is not accepted; no WP-1108 packaging changes are treated as a qualified prerequisite.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:66:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:72:- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:76:- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\ndocs/v…3921 tokens truncated…r request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:56:- **Scope:** Live operator sessions, interactive runs, autonomous tasks.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:106:  \"objective\": \"Verify that detached legacy client restore does not overwrite active leases.\",\ndocs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md:16:  for downstream units already existed before this work.\ndocs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md:84:- Token estimates are already heuristic; changing the budget model can shift every qualification timing. Record the\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:35:Nexus already produces structured turn data (`turn.execution`, `turn.outcome`, `turn.reason`, `turn.steps`) via `AutonomousAgent.runTurn`. LangSmith's trace model is a superset of this, organized hierarchically as runs within threads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:37:**Relevance to Nexus:** Nexus's `turn.ts` and `agent.ts` already emit structured per-turn events. Adopting a trace/span model (similar to OpenTelemetry semantics) would let Nexus capture the full execution tree of a turn — not just the final outcome, but every tool call, schema repair, and verifier invocation as nested spans.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:66:**Relevance to Nexus:** Nexus's `eval/score.mjs` already produces pooled metrics (`correct`, `rate`, `ci`, `falseVerified`), but lacks experiment versioning and side-by-side comparison. Adopting the experiment model would let Nexus:\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:86:Nexus's `eval/run.mjs` already performs offline evaluation against `eval/tasks/`. LangSmith's model adds:\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:92:Nexus already runs 5 runs per task configuration (per DEC-05 thresholds) and measures false VERIFIED = 0, crash rate ≤ 2%, regression rate ≤ 5%. These map directly to LangSmith's offline evaluation model.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:108:LangSmith defines five evaluator types. Nexus already uses some implicitly; formalizing them would improve evaluation rigor.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:118:**Nexus parallel:** `repairJson` validation, `isKnownToolName` checks, `ALL_DIGITS_RE` validation. These are already implicit code evaluators but could be formalized as first-class evaluator functions with named scores.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:205:**Relevance to Nexus:** Rules could auto-escalate failing runs to an annotation queue, or trigger re-runs of failed tasks on infrastructure failures (Nexus already has `eval/infra.mjs` for this).\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:320:Nexus already has strong foundations (eval harness, scoring, independent acceptance). Adopting LangSmith's structured model — particularly versioned datasets, experiment comparison, annotation queues, and online evaluation — would move Nexus from ad-hoc qualification to a continuous quality assurance system suitable for production LLM agent deployment.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:86:  - `nexus.compaction.preserved_items_count`: Count of active messages retained\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:193:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:254:nexus replay <trace-id> [--verify-only] [--interactive]\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:30:| TUI operation pane and in-view decision interaction | Needs the Ratatui surface and a PTY qualification matrix; the CLI view already covers the operator need | v1.2 (DEC-V11-14) |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:45:2. Verifier and baseline gates: no unit completes without the evidence the unit model already requires.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:179:reserved = Map<resourceId, count>          // seeded with the slots already held by RUNNING units\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:216:| Scheduler exception | The batch is abandoned; every unit still `RUNNING` is reconciled by the next `run()`; the operation blocks with `NOT_CONVERGING` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:279:| non-integer / negative | The envelope gate already treats the record as corrupt; the operation gate MUST also reject it rather than assume 1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:296:    // absent v1.1 fields stay absent; readers already use ?? [] / ?? 1 defaults\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:307:- No unit is rewritten. `contextBudget`, `context`, `git`, `integrations` and `contextCheckpoints` already load\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:311:The envelope migration backup already applies because the envelope version is unchanged; therefore the operation\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:508:  **resume**, the undelivered set is re-rendered; a message already delivered is not repeated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md:623:`mergeOperationPolicy` (`operation_cli.ts`) already merges config + spec. The new key follows the same precedence:\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:38:All G1 checks run under `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` / isolated `XDG_*` per CONCURRENCY §3; `npm --prefix cli test` already\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:12:conflict policy. `CandidateIdentity` already computed a content-addressed view of the working tree, which is the\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:32:   a time, in arrival order (v1.1.0: `OperationRunner.enqueueIntegration`). Dependency order is already guaranteed by\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:36:   `candidate`/`tests` when the worktree was already gone or the unit produced no verifier — an absent field is honest\ndocs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md:56:- Integration must not bypass the verification gates: a unit is integrated only with the evidence the unit model already\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793611690.2333965}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
