ck. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\n83:- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793613728.5597117}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
